    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">To bring sports cars into the world entails dangers and difficulties, unless they happen to be the scions of the big series. That can be entirely different as is most impressively illustrated by the history of the Porsche make. The main columns which the Porsche myth rests upon have undoubtedly been the 356 and 911 model ranges. That this is so an excellent reference for the product and the men behind it and apart from that, is a triumph of persistent evolution-also in esthetic terms. To report on and to pay homage to this and the Porsche cosmos in general is the main concern of this book.--book cover.</marc:subfield>
